#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494030} :activity/id #uuid "bba4c4cc-2793-5afd-91e2-7a137ae53cb5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494008 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ce7efb-3ad5-579b-809f-0dd2e31fe7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493451} {:answer/id #uuid "87f00bc1-a093-5b90-a9c9-83e2777d88d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493604} {:answer/id #uuid "aca0bca7-0e7a-58b7-a3c4-843dab2110e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493662} {:answer/id #uuid "be1fae9a-76f7-5ae7-af20-eb786be794c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493703} {:answer/id #uuid "f14395c6-36b4-5cb6-8085-7a9935a781a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493451} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ce3e2a-2275-50a0-b25b-b9f3436f743c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3ec301c4-26d6-5f2a-9132-b21928f5ee67" :question/math-academy-id "q-94638" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,3]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,3]\\to R$ and its subset $N$ containing all functions that return a nonzero value at exactly one point in $[0,3].$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $N$ is closed under function addition\n\nII. $N$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $N$ is a subspace of $C[0,3]$\n\nIV. $N$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,3]$\n\n*Hint: Different functions from $N$ might give a nonzero value at different points in $[0,3].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f({a}_{1})\\ne 0$ and $g({a}_{2})\\ne 0,$ where ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are distinct points in $[0,3],$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({a}_{1})+g({a}_{1}) & \\ne 0 \\\\ f({a}_{2})+g({a}_{2}) & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)+g(x)\\ne 0$ at two distinct points. So, $N$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(a)\\ne 0$ for some $a\\in [0,3],$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\n$$\n\n \nfor any $x\\in [0,3].$ So, $N$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $N$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""} :step/id #uuid "61b43f65-40c4-5ee2-a729-b625837e3d66" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494067}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494029 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b3a3727-45a2-5fb4-95ae-a91e8f4f3239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451353} {:answer/id #uuid "560e913c-ce8a-5991-9d57-1efe0344f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354} :answer-field/id #uuid "7994875a-855a-584f-b0b1-e9adddf96e49" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71e555b-f6a2-5bfa-a969-f07e226574ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451355} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe4cba6-6e86-5be1-8135-57a663228532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451356} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae639aa0-32cb-59c4-89fa-57a75c8e85c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d934afb8-4872-512d-b557-15198d1a48a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451357} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f2982f-15e7-58c5-94f1-438da460594b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451358} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a8d921-2a8a-515d-b4dc-86f366326881" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc6f1bb2-59b1-5487-b01f-c8947e4f8b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451359} {:answer/id #uuid "ee66f17e-227c-5e22-9f23-dbee97ac1f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451360}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186451359} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9876e54-bdbd-59af-a25c-ae629c2446e5" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ed6c488-d6f4-5c35-b1ec-2f3c2d68e465" :question/math-academy-id "q-43779" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-1,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-1,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[-1,1]\\,|\\,f(1)=f(-1)}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of $C[-1,1]$\n- **IV.** $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-1,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(1) & =f(1)+g(1) \\\\  & =f(-1)+g(-1) \\\\  & =(f+g)(-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(1) & =kf(1) \\\\  & =kf(-1) \\\\  & =(kf)(-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $B$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "876842ab-2531-5a55-8715-683cc46f3d77" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494008}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494030 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8536f8a6-1bfc-5275-95ca-8a1fda0afe28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123525} {:answer/id #uuid "b659c777-4549-54ab-9f1f-bae85db6256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123526} {:answer/id #uuid "5da722ba-7c66-52bf-862c-fc5ad59257b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123527} {:answer/id #uuid "64f059cc-f403-5120-b592-b5803d968b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} {:answer/id #uuid "79c277c4-a05b-5a16-ab06-0142128ff522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} :answer-field/id #uuid "856e0bc2-ed8c-5746-a814-6831d1a835e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "027d54ca-a5e1-5f8e-b0e8-aea8a3580062" :question/math-academy-id "q-43770" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a\\in R\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "87d932f6-49ba-5c24-8d19-a6ad3580ecf9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494029}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494067 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991f2f73-ac23-5191-ab80-7de9efee7e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452009} {:answer/id #uuid "2ead1013-7e82-50d2-9ea0-c2b7d5a04066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010} :answer-field/id #uuid "506cf49e-9f52-5299-8ed3-6ff8e24478db" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fed6d2ec-aee8-5542-8372-ae559f20b93f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452011} {:answer/id #uuid "c05c0c3e-d50a-5489-b880-65368c86a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6ad786-f4e4-5537-b235-5beb1d76d0c8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1613e4-3825-5163-955a-c508dc5a7424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452013} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4d7ea-1e52-5939-b1ad-c82fa09897e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014} :answer-field/id #uuid "860bab32-e063-5c7b-9daf-21735a207ce5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902ecaea-e103-52f1-8446-e92ffd5c7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} {:answer/id #uuid "b5359c31-2887-5291-8d2f-9c2c74acea93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} :answer-field/id #uuid "063b6651-61e1-5617-8f54-44670f58aa5b" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "44096d11-ac2c-5302-8668-0431e5543e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94642" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-2,2]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ and its subset $E$ containing all even functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $E$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n- **IV.** $E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(-x) & =f(-x)+g(-x) \\\\  & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =(f+g)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(-x) & =kf(-x) \\\\  & =kf(x) \\\\  & =(kf)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "ef5989bf-617a-54c7-bbc7-9e531c1f1c5b"}] :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493386}]}
